When a checkable editable gets focus, Ladybird checks all of its
existing text. Blink does the same, in its ColdModeSpellCheckRequester.
And Gecko’s mozInlineSpellChecker::EditorSpellCheckInited() checks the
whole text of an editor once spellchecking starts for it. But WebKit’s
HTMLTextFormControlElement::effectiveSpellcheckAttributeChanged() checks
a whole text control only when its spellcheck state changes — and
otherwise, WebKit checks each word only as the caret leaves that word.
